<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">29 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 29 June, from 626 to 1995.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantinople.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/626">626 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,400 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Avars and Persians begin their assault on Constantinople</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 80,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a>, allied with the Sasanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a>, began a coordinated assault on the walls of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, defended by some 12,000 Byzantine troops. After a month of bombardment, with their fleets sunk, the attackers abandoned the siege.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1072">1072 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">954 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The former emperor Romanos IV Diogenes is blinded</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The former emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanos-iv-diogenes">Romanos IV Diogenes</a> had agreed to resign and enter a monastery in return for his life, but the caesar John Doukas broke the agreement and had him blinded at Kotyaion. He died in exile soon afterwards.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanos-iv-diogenes">Romanos IV Diogenes</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1149">1149 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">877 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nur al-Din defeats and kills Raymond of Poitiers at Inab</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-crusade">Second Crusade</a>, the Zengid army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nur-al-din">Nur al-Din</a> Zengi destroyed the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raymond-of-poitiers">Raymond of Poitiers</a>, Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/order-of-assassins">Assassins</a> of Ali ibn-Wafa at Inab. Raymond was killed, and Antioch's eastern border was pushed west.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raymond-of-poitiers">Raymond of Poitiers</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1444">1444 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">582 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Skanderbeg defeats an Ottoman army at Torvioll</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Leading the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-lezhe">League of Lezhë</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a> defeated an Ottoman army under Ali Pasha at Torvioll in Albania, attacking its flanks and rear with troops hidden in the woods. It was his first major victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-torvioll">Battle of Torvioll</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1613">1613 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">413 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Globe Theatre burns down during Henry VIII</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a> fired for a stage effect set the thatched roof alight, and Shakespeare's playhouse burned to the ground within an hour. No one was killed, and it was rebuilt the next year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Spanish found Mission San Francisco de Asís</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Franciscan friars celebrated the first Mass at the mission later known as Mission <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dolores-hidalgo">Dolores</a>, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> expanded northward in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>. The settlement grew into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-francisco">San Francisco</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1855">1855 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">171 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Daily Telegraph is first published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Daily <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">Telegraph</a> and Courier appeared in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. Under new owners it soon became a penny paper and for a time had the largest circulation in the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">Telegraph</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1916">1916 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Roger Casement is sentenced to death for treason</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Irish nationalist and former British diplomat was condemned for seeking German help for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-rising">Easter Rising</a>. Despite pleas for clemency he was hanged in August.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1995">1995 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">31 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sampoong Department Store collapses in Seoul</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The five-storey store fell in seconds, killing 502 people. Investigators found illegal alterations and ignored warnings, prompting reforms of South Korean building safety.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 29 June <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/petronilla-of-aragon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/petronilla-of-aragon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Petronilla of Aragon</span><span class="tp">1136–1173</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-ii-of-aragon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-ii-of-aragon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John II of Aragon</span><span class="tp">1398–1479</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-washington-goethals"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-washington-goethals.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George Washington Goethals</span><span class="tp">1858–1928</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/robert-schuman"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/robert-schuman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Robert Schuman</span><span class="tp">1886–1963</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ernesto-perez-balladares"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ernesto-perez-balladares.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ernesto Pérez Balladares</span><span class="tp">b. 1946</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gurbanguly-berdimuhamedow"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gurbanguly-berdimuhamedow.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gurbanguly Berdimuhamedow</span><span class="tp">b. 1957</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 29 June <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/raymond-of-poitiers"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/raymond-of-poitiers.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Raymond of Poitiers</span><span class="tp">c. 1115–1149</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/abel-king-of-denmark"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abel-king-of-denmark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Abel, King of Denmark</span><span class="tp">1218–1252</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/janus-of-cyprus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/janus-of-cyprus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Janus of Cyprus</span><span class="tp">1375–1432</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-friedrich-karl-vom-stein"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/heinrich-friedrich-karl-vom-stein.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Heinrich Friedrich Karl vom Stein</span><span class="tp">1757–1831</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lucien-bonaparte"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lucien-bonaparte.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lucien Bonaparte</span><span class="tp">1775–1840</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-austria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-i-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ferdinand I of Austria</span><span class="tp">1793–1875</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
